## --- AsyncOpenFuture (B4) ------------------------------------------
##
## open(2) is non-blocking on regular files even without O_NONBLOCK,
## and our paths *will* be regular files in the 4B fixtures, so this
## future performs the open on its first poll and returns Ready. The
## async wrapper exists for surface symmetry with AsyncTcpStream.connect
## (which genuinely blocks pending TCP handshake completion).
##
## State: the `path` and `flags` the open uses, stored by `init`; `poll`
## performs the open and hands its result to the caller. The future owns
## its fields, so the result is built in `poll` rather than stored and
## moved out of a field. There is no reactor registration because the
## open call never returns EAGAIN.
class AsyncOpenFuture
  path: String
  flags: Int
  include Future
  type Output = Result[AsyncFile, IoError]

  def init(path: &String, flags: Int)
    self.path = path.clone
    self.flags = flags
  end

  def var poll(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Result[AsyncFile, IoError]]
    Poll.Ready(ruxen_async_file_open(self.path, self.flags))
  end
end
